rence to AI-driven job displacement, within the broad AI and ML shelf scope.", "video_id": "2081000627354681344"}, {"candidate_paths": [], "disposition": "existing_concept", "evidence": [{"card_hash": "9dbd09043b74d6030453cbe31c2caa48dbc678ef0b598f7c4f48732c511abe11", "excerpt_id": "9abbc53706abfb58416d0c3c2c6a2f83ae444dcc4030ee28f71e73e0e812794a", "quote": "An autonomous fighting robot tried to runway from a cage fight", "source_revision": "28f7ca02f966eedeb20759ce07db651ca2e45b6039df64a0955157ce3ad956fa", "video_id": "2081023025714188288"}], "existing_shelf_ids": ["ai-and-ml"], "reason": "Matches the 'autonomous systems' include cue of the AI and ML shelf.", "video_id": "2081023025714188288"}]}, {"candidates": [{"definition": "This shelf collects AI-powered products, model releases, and demos that generate or reinterpret creative media (video, avatars, games, and film) directly from prompts or scripts for end users and creators.", "exclude": ["foundation-model architecture, scaling-law, or open-weights discussion with no creative output shown", "IDE- or SDK-level coding-assistant tooling aimed at software engineering workflows", "space or astronomy content that has no AI-generation angle"], "include": ["AI avatar/digital-twin video generation products aimed at end users (e.g., Gemini Omni turning a script into a talking avatar)", "AI video-generation model releases explicitly marketed for creating content (e.g., Dreamina Seedance 2.5)", "No-code builders for multimodal AI companions/PALs that see, hear, act, and remember", "Frontier AI models demonstrated by generating game or interactive creative content rather than being benchmarked", "AI reinterpretations or remakes of existing film/media concepts (e.g., a classic sci-fi film redone with AI)"], "path": ["AI and ML", "Generative Media"], "sibling_cues": [{"confusing_alternative": "Frontier Models (multimodal model releases)", "evidence_needed": "card must describe an end-user creative output (a video/avatar being produced), not model architecture or benchmark numbers", "include_cue": "AI avatar/digital-twin video generation products aimed at end users"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Frontier Models (model capability release)", "evidence_needed": "card frames the release around creation/production use rather than technical capability comparison", "include_cue": "AI video-generation model releases marketed for creating content"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Developer Tools (agent harnesses)", "evidence_needed": "card emphasizes no-code/consumer-facing framing rather than SDK, IDE, or engineering workflow language", "include_cue": "No-code builders for multimodal AI companions/PALs"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Developer Tools (coding assistants writing code)", "evidence_needed": "card highlights the generated creative artifact itself (a game, a character) rather than the coding process or tool used to build it", "include_cue": "Frontier models demonstrated by generating game/interactive content"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Space and Science (space content)", "evidence_needed": "card discusses AI-driven filmmaking/generation, not actual astronomy, spacecraft, or scientific content", "include_cue": "AI reinterpretations of existing film/media"}], "supporting_evidence": [{"card_hash": "d8f9fc8caa3267f6cfc6cfd18536b6bff59f89f772e1f78ae84d724b4779c8e4", "excerpt_id": "416f4e399f79bb65aeaf4d890ad51ed345c76482acd6001fc96121c8d8f59b2f", "quote": "a new kind of application that sees, hears, acts, remembers, and emotionally understands you", "source_revision": "d1d8481a434aef66ec0621c098c6183e126127a83d6cc76836ba906f5e1c283a", "video_id": "2082506081365008384"}, {"card_hash": "84f3facb4018bc86b2031bf26457264494b7925d46b79fe160152fe250546d9a", "excerpt_id": "153d08f252ba46166171c822bcb20f084f87d24d649ca690e4790eeb377b78e9", "quote": "Gemini Omni in Google Vids lets you generate a personal AI avatar to star in your videos.", "source_revision": "fd5a8ca515b5a1eb307b9ab5d60b843371c882599aca