rative reviews of competing agent platforms as general-purpose digital teammates", "Speculative descriptions of always-on AI assistants continuously watching screens or meetings"], "path": ["AI and ML", "AI Agents"], "sibling_cues": [{"confusing_alternative": "AI Industry and Business (a company's AI-driven growth story)", "evidence_needed": "Quote must describe the agent performing the task (selling, underwriting) rather than investor/market commentary about the company", "include_cue": "Autonomous agents running end-to-end business operations"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Developer Tools (coding assistant)", "evidence_needed": "Quote must show the bot acting on general business tasks (NDAs, headcount), not code editors or IDEs", "include_cue": "AI bots that log into tools and complete tasks independently"}, {"confusing_alternative": "AI Industry and Business (marketing claim about a product)", "evidence_needed": "Quote must center on the agent's autonomous behavior/workflow execution, not pricing or company positioning", "include_cue": "Agents that learn workflows and operate unattended"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Developer Tools (coding assistant comparison)", "evidence_needed": "Quote must compare agent platforms as general-purpose 'teammates' even if coding tools are named as competitors", "include_cue": "Comparative reviews of competing agent platforms"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Frontier Models (capability/architecture speculation)", "evidence_needed": "Quote must frame the capability as an agent continuously doing real-world work, not a benchmark or scaling claim", "include_cue": "Speculative always-on AI assistants monitoring screens/meetings"}], "supporting_evidence": [{"card_hash": "d4956fcbcdd7ae0a300cb3d396f831573c3726736fa8c0bae26817b912b7a47e", "excerpt_id": "d65ff5aa3e6e902f21a0f4c381d44ac293c9e0f1657af6688c160cf79e6b8c66", "quote": "AI agents at Kavak sell the cars, underwrite the loans, coach the mechanics, and in one Mexican city, run the enti